{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["This passage was written to inform us that the Holy One, blessed be He, saved His servant and redeemed him from the hand of one stronger than him, and sent an angel and delivered him. And it further teaches us that he did not rely on his own righteousness, but exerted himself in every way he could to save himself. And it also contains a hint for all generations: everything that happened to our father with Esau his brother will always happen to us with the children of Esau, and it is fitting for us to follow the way of the righteous, who prepares himself with the three things with which he prepared himself — prayer, and a gift, and deliverance by way of war, to flee and to escape. And our Rabbis already saw this hint from this passage, as I shall mention (below, 32:9; 33:15):" "<b>To Esau his brother, to the land of Seir</b> — Because the south of the land of Israel is adjacent to Edom, and his father dwells in the land of the Negev, he must pass through Edom or close by there; therefore he feared lest Esau hear and come first against him, so he sent messengers to his land. And the Sages already seized upon him for this, saying in Bereshit Rabbah (Bereshit Rabbah 75:3): 'Grasping the ears of a dog' (Proverbs 26:17), etc. — the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: He was walking on his way and you were sending to him and saying to him, 'Thus says your servant Jacob.' And in my opinion this too alludes to the fact that we ourselves initiated our fall into the hand of Edom, for the kings of the Second Temple entered into a covenant with the Romans (I Maccabees 8), and some of them went to Rome (thus Ramban writes in Leviticus 26:16), and that was the cause of their fall by their hand. And this is mentioned in the words of our Rabbis and is well known in the books (Josippon, chapter 65):"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:38:29.986946112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}